  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Goliaths first appeared as a playable race in the DnD 3.5 supplement Races of Stone, and made their first appearance in 5th edition in the Elemental Evil Player’s Companion, making them one of the first non-core playable races in 5e. Much like dragonborn are a humanoid dragon, goliaths are a humanoid giant. That’s a weird statement to make since giants are basically just tall humanoids, but they’re a separate creature type. Still, the appeal of being almost Large size has remained appealing since the goliath’s first appearance. Goliaths do have fun and unique background lore, but generally players pick the Goliath because they want to be really big."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Mechanically, the Goliath is a spectacular option for any Strength-based\n\tbuild. Proficiency in Athletics gives you a staple option for many\n\tStrength-based characters and Stone’s Endurance provides a powerful defensive\n\toption which remains useful throughout your character’s career. Unfortunately,\n\tthese capabilities also pigeon-hole the Goliath into Strength-based melee\n\tbuilds. The custom origin rules and the updated version of the Goliath\n\tpublished in Mordenkainen Presents Monster’s the Multiverse open up your\n\tability score options, allowing you to bring the durability of Stone’s\n\tEndurance to any build."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you’re using the version of the Goliath originally published in the\n\tElemental Evil Player’s Companion, note that the Goliath’s Mountain Born trait\n\thas been updated to add resistance to cold damage. This change was made in\n\tIcewind Dale: Rime of the Frostmaiden, and in errata documents and the Sage\n\tAdvice Compendium."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
